HST Office: menu items show LibreOffice's own icons in every HST icon style.

Reason: owner decision of 20/11/2026. Menu icons (context menus, menu bar, drop-down menus) reuse the
LibreOffice (Colibre) icons at their right size, so they stay as sharp as upstream; the HST glyphs
stay on the ribbon and the frame. Until now a menu took the command's icon from the current style:
the Cổ điển style forced its Find and Replace glyphs into the menus (they replace Colibre's on the
ribbon), and the Hiện đại style put an HST glyph on every command it draws.
MenuBarManager::FillMenuImages now asks framework::GetMenuImageForCommand. Its order in the HST
styles: an image the user (Tools > Customize, module image manager user layer) or the document
assigned to the command; then "cmd/sc_<command>.png" from colibre_svg / colibre_dark_svg at the
display's icon scale (vcl::CommandInfoProvider::GetLibreOfficeMenuImage; the 150 % rule of
hst-icon-theme-fractional-scale.patch applies); then the style's own image (GetImageForCommand),
which serves the commands Colibre does not draw. Commands with arguments and every non-HST theme keep
upstream's lookup. framework::ImageManager::hasUserImage tells a user image from a theme default.

Applies after hst-icon-theme-fractional-scale.patch.
Test: make CppunitTest_vcl_app_test (test_HstIconTheme: MenusUseLibreOfficeIcons) and
make CppunitTest_framework_menuimages.
License: upstream files remain MPL-2.0.
